Prepare a bounded, source-versioned evidence slice for interpretOffers. Translate surplus descriptions into functional properties, quantities, condition, and known limitations. Distinguish verified specifications from seller assumptions, preserve ownership and handling restrictions, and identify information needed before proposing a consequential reuse. Include direct observations, current authority, contrary evidence, a plausible rival interpretation, and missing decisive fields. Carry forward the actual prior-stage records when provided.
